  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 343 AM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nThe light at the end of this hot tunnel is in sight. Cluster\nanalysis continues to show uncertainty on the speed of the front\nwith much cooler temperatures behind it. The relief will begin\nin northern MO on Sunday during the day and is expected to be\ncompletely through the area by Tuesday. Current NBM guidance\ninterquartile range for the high temperatures on Monday reaches\n10 degrees due to the uncertainty in the fronts exact position\nand speed. Behind the front temperatures are expected to be much\ncooler, and latest NBM guidance continues to trend cooler than\nprevious days. For example, NBM has dropped Tuesday max\ntemperature forecasts around 8 degrees over the last 48 hours,\nnow with highs only in the upper 60s to low 70s. This air mass\nwill dominate for the rest of the week with a gradual warming\nthrough the 70s.\n\nThe highest chance for showers and thunderstorms in the next\nweek will be Sunday night into Monday morning behind the cold\nfront. While the confidence is low on the exact timing and\nlocation of this convection, there is a 60-80% chance across the\nregion of measurable rainfall during this period, and 30-60%\nchance of seeing 0.25 inches of rain.",
